schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Finding Your People
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: framework
  summary: >-
    A member-attraction framework for local regen node builders: define your
    ideal member (values, skills, contribution, needs) and your non-ideal
    member before looking; look in named online spaces (Discord, Twitter/X,
    Reddit, LinkedIn) and offline spaces (local meetups, co-working spaces,
    community events, university groups); attract people through content
    marketing, community presence, events, and one-on-one relationships;
    and move them through a four-stage funnel (Awareness, Interest, Visit,
    Join) toward what ultimately attracts people to stay — authenticity,
    belonging, purpose, and value.
  audience: local regen node builders/organizers
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      Uses explicit marketing-funnel language ("Content Marketing," "The
      Funnel," attracting an "ideal member") for what is otherwise framed
      elsewhere on the site as organic, trust-based community building — the
      instrumental framing sits in tension with the site's broader
      anti-extractive posture (see the "Know Your Non-Ideal" step, which
      itself gates who belongs).
  related_concepts:
    - community-member-attraction-funnel
  related_resources: []
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/finding-your-people.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted

